The Project Management team is at the center of agency operations, connecting people, processes, and priorities to keep work moving forward. We are strategic problem solvers and trusted partners who collaborate across functions to deliver high-quality work on time and within budget. &nbsp;

Position Summary &nbsp;

The Associate Project Manager partners with Project Managers and agency departments to manage projects. &nbsp;

Essential Functions of the job include but are not limited to:

Project Planning &nbsp;
Responsible for partnering with the Project Managers and Sr. Project Managers to: &nbsp;

• Assist &nbsp;in basic project planning and execution of work &nbsp;

• Learn how to obtain a clear understanding of client expectations and rules of engagement &nbsp;

• Develop skills to build actionable project plans and vet through key team members &nbsp;

Meeting Management &nbsp;

• Attend and schedule internal meetings, including kickoff, internal review, regroup, and status &nbsp;

• Take notes and provide recaps and next steps to attendees &nbsp;

Workflow / Process &nbsp;

• Understand and advocate for the workflow process and each team member’s role and responsibility within the workflow &nbsp;

• Review action orders (AOs) to ensure a clear and executable direction is provided &nbsp;

• Lead the online routing of projects, while ensuring quality assurance at each step &nbsp;

• Maintain the daily hot sheet &nbsp;

Communication &nbsp;

• Provide constant communication in person, via email, IM, phone, etc., to meet client expectations and deliverables &nbsp;

• Advocate for the team while&nbsp; monitoring &nbsp;delivery dates &nbsp;

• Hold proactive,&nbsp; positive &nbsp;and good communications with multiple team members in varying departments &nbsp;

